Build the turboquant AVX-512 VNNI paths without the VNNI intrinsics.

qdrant 1.18's `quantization` crate calls `_mm512_dpbusd_epi32` and
`_mm512_dpwssd_epi32`. LLVM 22 changed the operand types of
`llvm.x86.avx512.vpdpbusd.512` (`<16 x i32>` -> `<64 x i8>`) and
`llvm.x86.avx512.vpdpwssd.512` (`<16 x i32>` -> `<32 x i16>`), and rustc
1.97's bundled stdarch emits the new form. nixpkgs still builds rustc
against llvmPackages_21 (llvm 21.1.8), which declares the old form, so
codegen aborts with:

  error: intrinsic signature mismatch for `llvm.x86.avx512.vpdpbusd.512`:
    expected `<16 x i32> (<16 x i32>, <16 x i32>, <16 x i32>)`,
    found    `<16 x i32> (<16 x i32>, <64 x i8>, <64 x i8>)`

This is a nixpkgs packaging bug, not a qdrant one: stock `nixpkgs.qdrant`
fails the same way, and qdrant master still calls the same intrinsics, so
no version bump escapes it. The upstream fix is NixOS/nixpkgs#544495
("rust_1_97: build against LLVM 22"), open against staging as of
2026-08-22. nixpkgs already carries the same class of workaround for other
crates -- see NixOS/nixpkgs#538998 (vectorchord) and #541607 (mistral-rs).

Delete this patch once the flake's nixpkgs pin has `rustc.llvmPackages.llvm`
at 22 or newer (i.e. once #544495, or a tree-wide default LLVM bump, has
landed). Check with:
  nix-instantiate '<nixpkgs>' -A rustc.llvmPackages.llvm

The shims are exact rather than approximations, and qdrant's own
`test_avx512_vnni_matches_scalar` tests run them against the scalar
reference during the build on any AVX-512 VNNI host.
